THPPlugin calls into the Python API without holding the GIL. Most of the calls look benign (read-only access), but it probably should be cleaned up:
...
        Py_UNBLOCK_THREADS;
        THTensor_(set)(LIBRARY_STATE ((THPTensor*)self)->cdata, ((THPTensor*)PyTuple_GET_ITEM(args, 0))->cdata);
        Py_BLOCK_THREADS;
...

Not super important, but might be useful to have those logical operators in the core.
As a workaround implementation, they can be simulated with current functions. For example
-- t1 and t2 are ByteTensors with 0 or 1 only
function tensor_and(t1, t2)
  return (t1 + t2):eq(2)
end
